{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh also called for the wise men.</b> The astrologers." "<b>And the sorcerers.</b> Those who alter the natural order for the eye's perception." "And the hartumim: they are those who know the secret of nature. And the fourth word perhaps is the language of Egypt, or the language of Chaldea, for we do not find it in all of Scripture except in the words of both of them. And Scripture distinguished between the deed of Moses, which was truth — the staff turned into a serpent — and the deed of the hartumim. Therefore it is written בלטיהם, and the third word [חרטומים] is from the root of להט החרב (Genesis 3:24), אשכבה לוהטים (Psalms 57:5), \"ולהט אותם היום הבא\" (Malachi 3:19), and it is like flashing and fire passing through; and this is sleight of hand."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {2 "The comment identifies 'the third word' as חרטומים by deriving it from the root להט, while 'the fourth word' refers to an element within that word whose origin is uncertain (Egyptian or Chaldean). The phrase 'in the words of both of them' is ambiguous but likely refers to Egyptians and Chaldeans."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:25.031862862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}